<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc in China animal nutrition pact.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc in China animal nutrition pact.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Animal Nutrition said Tuesday that it and China's Tianjin Bohai Chemical Industry Co Ltd  have agreed to create a joint venture in methionine, an amino-acid used as a nutritional additive in poultry feed.</p>
<p>The new company, called Bohai (Tianjin) Rhone-Poulenc Methionine Co Ltd, will have registered capital of RMB300 million, or US$36 million.</p>
<p>Bohai Chemical will hold 70 percent of the shares, Rhone-Poulenc Animal Nutrition 20 percent and Rhone-Poulenc (China) Co Ltd 10 percent.</p>
</text>
